✗ the handler reaches a driver

    internal/modules/orders/application/place.go:3
      package example.com/fix/internal/modules/orders/application          (layer: application)
        ↳ example.com/fix/internal/store
        imports github.com/jackc/pgx/v5

  A use case says WHAT must happen, never HOW it is stored, and that holds
  through a helper as much as directly: this package does not import
  github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 itself, but everything it depends on comes with it.

  The import is in example.com/fix/internal/store.

  Fix one of:
    • SPLIT that package. The part the handler needs — an identifier, a
      decision, a plain value — is almost always driver-free; only the code
      that talks to the store needs github.com/jackc/pgx/v5.
      Two packages, and the handler imports the half without it.
    • If the handler needs the STORE, declare a port in the domain and put
      the driver code in infrastructure, where a driver is allowed.
      `warren g repository` writes both halves.

1 violation(s) in 2 packages.

  Checked 1 feature module for cross-module imports.
